@startuml read-path-pruning-decode
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #534AB7
  BackgroundColor #EEEDFE
  FontColor #26215C
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #888780
  BackgroundColor #F1EFE8
  FontColor #2C2C2A
}

title labukDB — Read Path: Pruning (planner/) + Decode (decode/)\nCopyright 2026 Afzal and lakehouse-flight contributors — Apache 2.0

[Snapshot / NormalizedSnapshot\n(live file set + schema,\nfrom log/ or format/)] as SNAP

package "planner/ — pruning (no file opened yet)" #EEEDFE {
  [QueryPlanner\n(plan() for Delta's Snapshot;\nplanNormalized() for any\nTableFormat's NormalizedSnapshot)] as QP
  [PartitionPruner\n(① exact match on partition\nvalues from the log -- no I/O)] as PP
  [FileStatsPruner\n(② range check on add.stats\nmin/max from the log -- no I/O;\nIceberg's DataFileRef.getStats()\nis always null today -- no\ncolumn-stats pruning for Iceberg yet)] as FSP
  [PartitionValueSubstituter\n(folds partition predicate\nclauses to constants per file)] as PVS
  [PredicateColumns\n(collects columns referenced\nin the predicate tree)] as PC
  [ScanPlan / NormalizedScanPlan\n(surviving files + residual\npredicate + skip count)] as SCANPLAN
}

package "decode/ — Parquet → Arrow (file now opened)" #EEEDFE {
  [ParquetToArrowReader\n(local File or remote\nHadoop InputFile)] as PTAR
  [RowGroupPruner\n(③ Parquet footer stats --\none file open, header only)] as RGP
  [GroupPredicateEvaluator\n(④ per-row residual filter,\nfused with decode -- failing\nrows never enter Arrow vectors)] as GPE
  [PartitionValueAppender\n(fills partition columns as\nconstants -- not in the\nphysical Parquet file)] as PVA
  [NestedTypeDecoder\n(LIST/MAP/STRUCT, any nesting\ndepth -- read side)] as NTD
  [Int96TimestampCodec\n(legacy Spark timestamp\nencoding -> Instant UTC)] as ITC
  [DecimalCodec\n(Decimal128, precision<=38;\nshared with encode/)] as DCC
  [ParquetFooterCache\n(schema cached per stable\nlocal path)] as PFC
}

SNAP --> QP
QP --> PP : ① partition values
QP --> FSP : ② file stats min/max
QP --> PVS : fold partition predicates\nper file, before decode
QP --> PC : collect predicate columns\nfor safe projection
QP --> SCANPLAN

SCANPLAN --> PTAR : one call per\nsurviving file

PTAR --> RGP : ③ skipNextRowGroup()\nfor pruned row groups
PTAR --> GPE : ④ residual filter,\nfused with decode
PTAR --> PVA : reconstruct partition\ncolumns as constants
PTAR --> NTD : decode LIST/MAP/STRUCT\ncolumns
PTAR --> ITC : decode INT96 timestamps
PTAR --> DCC : decode DECIMAL\n(4 legal physical encodings)
PTAR --> PFC : cache schema by path\n(local only)

note bottom of SCANPLAN
  Four pruning levels, cheapest first --
  ①② never open a file at all; ③ opens
  one file's footer only; ④ is fused with
  decode itself, zero extra materialization.
end note

note bottom of NTD
  Recursive dispatcher (SQL engine session's
  own prior work, separate from Phase 1's
  SQL-IR work): any depth of LIST/MAP/STRUCT
  nesting, four leaf primitive kinds
  (float/double/int32/int64/string).
  Decimal/timestamp/boolean leaves inside a
  nested position are a separate, not-yet-
  wired expansion -- deliberately, to avoid
  a schema that builds but a reader that
  can't actually decode it.
end note

note right of PTAR
  The projection-pushdown fix this project
  found the hard way: the physical read set
  is OUTPUT columns UNION predicate columns
  (via PredicateColumns.collect) -- a WHERE
  on a column not in the SELECT list used to
  throw InvalidRecordException before this,
  since the predicate referenced a column
  never decoded.
end note

@enduml
